# bf-cpu

bf-cpu is a cpu that runs brainf*ck as an instruction set, designed in
SystemVerilog.

## Specs

 * ROM / 64 KiB
 * RAM / 64 KiB
 * Cache / 64 KiB (for call stack)

## Simulation

bf-cpu has been tested in simulation, but not real hardware.  Verilator is the
recommended tool for synthesization and simulation.  To synthesize all modules,
run

```sh
$ make all
```

Optionally, run all testbenches on the build with

```sh
$ make test
```

To simulate the cpu, run

```sh
$ make test_bf_cpu
```

### Running Other Programs

The default ROM image is a ROT13 cipher program, contained in `rom_image.bf`.
To run a different program, replace the contents of that file and rebuild.

## Credit

The Brainf*ck programming language was originally created by Urban Mueller in
1993.

Everything in this repository not otherwise disclaimed was written by Ira
Parsons.  No LLMs were used at any point in this project.

